] Published: 10 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; The rainbow arborescence conjecture posits that if the arcs of a directed graph with $n$n vertices are colored by $n-1$n−1 colors such that each color class forms a spanning arborescence, then there is a spanning arborescence that contains exactly one arc of every color. ... This work has been merged with arXiv:2412.15457\n\nHome › Combinatorics › The Rainbow Arborescence Problem on Cycles\n\n# The Rainbow Arborescence Problem on Cycles\n\nCombinatorics 2025-12-10 v2 Discrete Mathematics\n\nAuthors: Kristóf Bérczi , Tamás Király , Yutaro Yamaguchi , Yu Yokoi\n\nView on arXiv ↗ PDF ↗\n\n### Abstract\n\nThe rainbow arborescence conjecture posits that if the arcs of a directed graph with $n$n vertices are colored by $n-1$n−1 colors such that each color class forms a spanning arborescence, then there is a spanning arborescence that contains exactly one arc of every color. We prove that the conjecture is true if the underlying undirected graph is a cycle.\n\n### Keywords\n\nrainbow arborescence directed graph spanning arborescence cycle graph coloring\n\n### Cite\n    \n    @article{arxiv.2511.04953,\n      title  = {The Rainbow Arborescence Problem on Cycles},\n      author = {Kristóf Bérczi and Tamás Király and Yutaro Yamaguchi and Yu Yokoi},\n      journal= {arXiv preprint arXiv:2511.04953},\n      year   = {2025}\n    }\n\n### Comments\n\nThis work has been merged with arXiv:2412.15457\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPublications – Kristóf Bérczi's homepage (https://berkri.web.elte.hu/index.php/publications/)\nciteturn1search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Yokoi, The rainbow arborescence problem on cycles, arXiv:2511.04953, 2025. ... Yokoi, Rainbow Arborescence Conjecture, arXiv:2412.15457, 2024.\n  8. K. Bérczi, T. Király, Y. Yamaguchi, Y. Yokoi, The rainbow arborescence problem on cycles, arXiv:2511.04953, 2025.\n  9. Y. Bai, K. Bérczi, J. K. Siemelink, A